//! Parity of fantasy models, cost models and the hypervolume knowledge
//! gradient with BoTorch (fixtures in `tests/fixtures/phase5c_hvkg/*.json`,
//! generated by `scripts/generate_fixtures.py --phase 5c-hvkg` with BoTorch
//! main and `--phase 5c-hvkg-prs` with BoTorch pull requests):
//!
//! * `condition_on_observations` of single- and multi-output `SingleTaskGP`s
//!   (inferred and fixed noise, `Normalize`, `Standardize`, batched
//!   observations) and of `ModelListGP`s, and `fantasize` (batched inputs,
//!   explicit observation noise, lists with shared or per-output samplers
//!   and evaluation masks): the joint posteriors of the conditioned and
//!   fantasy models (batched), with and without observation noise, with
//!   BoTorch's base samples;
//! * with meta-pytorch/botorch#3396 / #3399 (if the fixtures exist): explicit
//!   noise of homoskedastic models and lists with transforms;
//! * qHVKG and qMFHVKG values and gradients (posterior means and samples,
//!   `log`, `current_value`, pending points, evaluation masks, objectives,
//!   cost-aware utilities, target-fidelity projections) with BoTorch's base
//!   samples; the value function and `_split_hvkg_fantasy_points`;
//! * `optimize_acqf` of qHVKG from BoTorch's initial conditions (one restart
//!   per problem), and `gen_one_shot_hvkg_initial_conditions` from the same
//!   raw samples (if recorded);
//! * cost models, `InverseCostWeightedUtility`, `project_to_target_fidelity`
//!   and `expand_trace_observations`.
//!
//! Tolerances: posteriors and values 1e-9 (relative; log values absolute
//! below 1), gradients 1e-8 (relative to the largest component), costs and
//! projections 1e-12. Run with `--nocapture` to print the error tables.

